# Environment — EVERY env file is ignored, including the local-dev ones that
# used to be tracked. A file that is safe today acquires a real key the first
# time somebody points the checkout at something real, and by then it is
# already in the history. Templates are what ship; fill them in per machine:
#
#   cp apps/backend/.env.example  apps/backend/.env
#   cp apps/frontend/.env.example apps/frontend/.env.local
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

# Debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

